### Token Management System - REST API Tests
### Compatible with VS Code REST Client extension
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api
@jwtToken = {{login.response.body.jwt}}

### 1. Register Organizer
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dr. Sarah",
  "email": "sarah@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Login Organizer (Stores JWT for subsequent calls)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sarah@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Create an Event
# @name createEvent
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

{
  "title": "General OPD Consultation"
}

@eventId = {{createEvent.response.body._id}}

### 4. Get My Events
GET {{baseUrl}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

### 5. Get Event by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

### 6. Update Event Title
PUT {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

{
  "title": "General OPD - Room 101"
}

### 7. Public: Get Event Title (No login)
GET {{baseUrl}}/public/events/{{eventId}}

### 8. Public: Join Queue (Issue Token #1)
# @name joinQueue
POST {{baseUrl}}/public/events/{{eventId}}/join
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Smith"
}

@tokenId = {{joinQueue.response.body._id}}

### 9. Public: Join Queue Again (Issue Token #2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/public/events/{{eventId}}/join
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bob Johnson"
}

### 10. Public: Join with Empty Name (Should return 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/public/events/{{eventId}}/join
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": ""
}

### 11. Organizer: Get Tokens for Event (Sorted by arrival)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tokens?eventId={{eventId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

### 12. Organizer: Mark Token as Done
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tokens/{{tokenId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}

{
  "status": "done"
}

### 13. Organizer: Delete Event (Also deletes its tokens)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/events/{{eventId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{jwtToken}}
